WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:02.835
Hey YouTubers, it's Charlie.

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:05.415
So this is going to be my Gotham Episode 13 video.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:10.420
It was a good story that proved that the criminals aren't the only bad people in the city.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:15.820
Gotham in general is full of really crappy people, and this just put the focus more on people who you would

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:17.320
normally think are legit.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.680
So just careful for spoilers if you haven't seen the episode yet.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:20.980
Starting with Top 5 Moments: 

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:26.880
No. 5: Fish Mooney is plopped on the table like fresh fish getting ready to get carved up.

00:00:26.883 --> 00:00:30.963
I really love the spirit of this scene, although, there were some moments that got a little hammy.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.920
I've always felt like Jada Pinkett-Smith is channeling a little bit of Eartha Kitt in her performances.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.220
Which I think is totally appropriate for the setting.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:41.700
But when we see someone go into a torture chamber like that (a make-shift torture chamber) you're expecting to

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.180
see something from a "SAW" movie.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:44.840
Like some, crazy, torture porn.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:49.400
It's too bad the show isn't on basic cable, because some of those gratuitous shots, even Zsasz coming to 

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.640
clean up later would have been really effective.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:55.300
That's one of the things that shows like Game of Thrones has in it's favor, being on HBO.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.860
It can show you someone getting their head squished like a grape.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:02.780
So you get a lot of extra people talking about the show just because something SO crazy happened

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.400
that you would never expect on-screen.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.900
Generally you can't really do that with network shows, but Gotham gets pretty close.

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:12.400
I was kind of hoping, when Bob pulled out the power tools, that he'd draw a little blood. 

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:17.060
I feel like Jada Pinkett-Smith, she's a great actress, so she's be able to take it to that place. 

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:19.960
So it was a little bit of a bummer that they chose to play it safe.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:21.180
'Butch to the rescue'

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:23.700
Don't you just wonder what's going on between the two of them?

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:28.340
I feel like Fish Mooney has really close relationships with a lot of different people.

00:01:28.341 --> 00:01:29.460
And not just men.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:31.300
She had that weird connection with Liza.

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:36.300
Like she was trying to be her mother,  but she was more like her big sister, or even some sort of passive lover.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:40.740
Then you have her relationship with Butch which seams really close -- a really genuine friendship.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:43.840
I felt kinda bad after what happened to him, but I don't think he's dead.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:47.344
Add to that that Bullock looks like he really enjoys her flavor of fish.~

00:01:47.344 --> 00:01:49.140
You can make as many jokes about that as you want.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:50.735
'Bullock like fresh fish'

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:56.020
That Bullock scene at the end was actually really, probably, the most touching Fish-Mooney moment. 

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:58.639
She seemed much more like a person, and less like a comicbook villain.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:02.400
I really do want to learn more about what's going on between her and Bullock though.

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:06.400
No. 4: The Penguin's acid-trip victory montage.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.000
Of all the montages in the episode (there were several), this was the craziest.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:14.500
I almost put it on my Thumbs Down list, but it's one of those things that's so bad, that's it's good.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:16.760
It's almost like he's having a two minute orgasm.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.240
And that speech that he gives -- that was so funny. 

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:21.880
Like he just starts to go crazy, and Fish Mooney walks in.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:26.760
If you haven't read the comics, the Penguin actually does own his own club; it's called "The Iceberg Lounge".

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.160
And later it was renamed to, "The Iceberg Casino". He turned it into a casino.

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:34.340
There's a high-roller area in the back where super criminals go to meet. There's a resturaunt up top.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:39.860
As a character, the Penguin loves the trappings of high society, so owning an upscale club is totally natural 

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:40.780
for the character.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:43.220
Although the Penguin on this show is a long way out from that.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:46.760
Did anyone else spit out their drink whenever he was standing next to that big fish plaque?

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.540
That was just...it was just so ridiculous.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:49.780
But you love it so much.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.520
I totally don't mind when Gotham gets a little cheesy.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.480
As long as it leans into the curb.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:56.540
Having his mother around helps a lot too.

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:58.080
She is just so wild.

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:01.560
Whenever she met Gordon, I felt like she going to try and eat 'em alive.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:05.020
I'm more scared of her, than I am of any of the other villains on the show.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.820
No. 3: Victor Zsasz, cleans up the mess.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.080
It wouldn't be a party without mister 'no eyebrows'.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:12.080
That's actually a good way to creep people out:

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:13.280
just shave your eyebrows off.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:14.880
You'll ten times scarier. 

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:17.518
Not quite as scary as the Penguin's mother, but still pretty scary.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:21.100
Of all the montages in the episode, his felt like the most fun.

00:03:21.109 --> 00:03:23.980
Just because he felt like a steamroller (like he was unstoppable).

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:26.540
Somebody should tell him not to play with his food.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:30.800
I kinda wished that he would've finished off Butch, but I understand why they're keeping him on the show.

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:34.120
He's a fairly valuable character, especially when Fish Mooney is around

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:36.760
so they're going to want to bring him back in the back-half of the season.

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:41.060
I think that's why they gave him that 'antihero' escape moment earlier in the episode.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:43.880
Whenever he busted out of the back of the truck, Batman-style, and escaped.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.780
It's a fairly common shot, but anytime you see a character look one way, and then there's nothing --

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:52.600
and then look back and all of a sudden someone's there -- people just think that as Batman now.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.401
Like that's "Pulling a Batman" on someone.

00:03:54.401 --> 00:04:00.075
Anytime they give a character that kind of shot, like they give him that kind of moment, you know they're getting ready to do something bad ass.

00:04:00.075 --> 00:04:02.915
So I'm actually waiting for the Riddler to get a shot like that.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:03.840
That's what I want to see.

00:04:04.359 --> 00:04:06.324
No. 2: The Riddler and Ms. Kringle.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:11.160
What gives away really awesome gifts, and is probably going to go crazy before the end of this season?

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:13.900
Answer: The BEST character on this show.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:15.600
That might be a bit of a stretch.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:19.220
The Riddler might not be THE best character on the show, but he's definitely one of my favorites. 

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:24.760
Any character that can bounce back and forth really easily between crazy and funny...is AMAZING in my book.

00:04:24.762 --> 00:04:28.962
I think them adding this 'young love' dynamic to it makes it that much funnier too.

00:04:28.962 --> 00:04:35.413
Just the awkward component of him really liking Ms. Kringle, and all these other douchebag cops just stomping all over him.

00:04:35.413 --> 00:04:38.833
That's why I was kind of bummed at the end of the episode when Gordon took Flass down.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:41.540
I was kinda hoping that the Riddler was gonna do something crazy.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:45.245
Or that card that he left was going to turn out to be something a little more sinister.

00:04:45.245 --> 00:04:47.222
Like he was going to try and turn the tables on them.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:48.940
We're not to that territory yet.

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:51.700
And it actually seemed pretty hopeful the way they ended with Ms. Kringle.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:54.460
Looking at her character, like she hasn't had that many lines.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:58.000
I felt like her reaction was probably the best it could have possibly been.

00:04:58.186 --> 00:04:59.880
"Just don't...just don't speak!"

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:01.062
"Don't make it worse!"

00:05:01.062 --> 00:05:04.340
That moment almost felt uncomfortably autobiographical.

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:06.560
Who has NOT been in a situation like that?

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:10.200
And, my No. 1 moment: Gordon and Bullock vs. the Commissioner.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:14.364
Make no mistake, even though Flass was the criminal they arrested at the end of this episode

00:05:14.364 --> 00:05:15.627
...the Commissioner was the real villain.

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:19.780
The captain explained that all the steamrolling that happened to everyone in the episode

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:22.500
was because the Commissioner was putting his weight behind it.

00:05:22.757 --> 00:05:25.617
So the false report about the suicide: all Commissioner.

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:27.580
The stash houses and the dirty cops: 

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:28.580
Commissioner.

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:31.180
I don't think he's going to end up being the biggest villain of the season.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:32.680
I don't think it's going to be that simple.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:35.560
So now I'm actually wondering who he's working with.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:39.000
I wouldn't be surprised if it ends up being someone on the Wayne Board we haven't met yet.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.034
Someone behind the Venom precursor.

00:05:41.034 --> 00:05:45.114
When you look at the villains of this season, you have the street criminals (like Fish Mooney);

00:05:45.114 --> 00:05:45.914
you have the Mob.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:49.880
Then you have the white collar criminals, like the people in the Wayne Foundation and the Commissioner.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:52.260
People that work inside the government.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:55.140
It makes you wonder if there are any heroes in positions of power.

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:59.820
So don't be surprised if, in some big twist, Falcone ends up being one of the big protagonists. 

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:01.940
Even though, technically, he's one of the biggest villains.

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:05.200
That's one of the charms of Gotham, is that everyone is bad.

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:11.600
So when you try to differentiate between protagonist, and antagonist, you really end up picking from the same bucket.

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:13.020
Here's my big question for you guys:

00:06:13.021 --> 00:06:16.120
Who do you think is going to be the bigger villain at the end of the season?

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:18.838
Is it going to be the Commissioner, or is it going to be Falcone?

00:06:18.838 --> 00:06:21.858
I'm kinda hoping they don't roll out too many new characters.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:28.080
Usually you want to meet who all the important people are by the first-half of the season, or even in the first couple of episodes.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:33.619
I think the writers are still finding the voices of all the characters so it IS getting better with each episode.

00:06:33.619 --> 00:06:36.541
So I'm really optimistic for the last arc of the season.

00:06:36.541 --> 00:06:41.601
Usually what you get is too many arcs. You get like, a block of 3 or 4 episodes that tell a minor story.

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:44.300
Next week's episode is actually going to be a two-parter.

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:47.300
They will be doing a scarecrow-ish, type story.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:50.020
Like a 'Jonathan Crane/Fear Toxin' prequel story.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:52.380
Here's some of the bigger Easter eggs that I saw in the episode 

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:55.800
(but if you saw any that I don't mention, just feel free to write 'em in the comments):

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:59.897
So I already mentioned the Penguin's club, the Iceberg Lounge (or the Iceberg Casino).

00:06:59.897 --> 00:07:00.977
However you want to think about it.

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:02.600
We have the Riddler's notes.

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:03.686
He's already left clues.

00:07:03.686 --> 00:07:05.766
Now he's starting to leave his signature 'notes'.

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:10.760
When Alfred and Bruce are walking around, he tells them he's gonna get, "ripped to shreds" by the females.

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:13.460
But that just feels like a Catwoman fight, waiting to happen.

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:19.380
The drugs that Gordon finds aren't specified by name, but they remind me of the Venom derivative. 

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:23.478
It terms of really notable drugs, shows typically find something and stick with it.

00:07:23.478 --> 00:07:25.019
Like on Arrow for instance:

00:07:25.019 --> 00:07:27.780
They're sticking with Vertigo, even though they did it in Season 2.

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:32.220
I didn't see any Easter eggs during the Poison Ivy seen but you guys can let me know if you spotted any.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:35.200
Right at the end, Bruce actually talks about going to Switzerland.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:39.880
I'm trying to remember, I think that he actually battled Ra's al Ghul in Switzerland.

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:42.720
Like it was a part of a Ra's al Ghul story arc (in the Batman comics).

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:44.940
But somebody can feel free to correct me on that.

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:48.460
So as much fun as the episode was, there a couple of thumbs down I had.

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:50.160
A couple of things I felt just didn't work.

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:55.060
The Bruce Wayne/Catwoman scene at the end -- where she rejects him -- obviously very clearly likes

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:56.520
him so much that she's pushing him away.

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:58.160
I felt like that was a little forced.

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:01.060
Plus, Bruce crying later. Anything with Bruce crying...

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:02.080
 ...just get rid of that.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:04.000
I feel like it's just interminable. 

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:07.580
So, a couple awesome montages in the episode, but the first one where Gordon started to

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:10.620
question the police had this really weird music playing behind it.

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:13.920
Like it was meant to be funny, but it just ended up sounding a little weird.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:16.860
And then, the Penguin kissing Fish Mooney's feet.

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:21.600
That was another 'so bad that it's good' moment, but I put it on the Thumbs Down list just becuase

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:22.840
it was SO over the top. 

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:24.100
Like it was CRAZY.

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:25.460
You guys can let me know though:

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:28.720
I mean, do you like it when the show does REALLY crazy things? 

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:32.580
Where it's just like, "Okay, they're very clearly not taking themselves super seriously".

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:34.940
Sometimes it can be fun. Sometimes it doesn't work.

00:08:35.540 --> 00:08:36.380
So, big stuff:

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:40.900
Next week is gonna be the part of a two-part episode, so be sure to subscribe to get that.

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:44.480
New episode of The Flash tomorrow, and then a new episode of Arrow.

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:48.320
There've been some liberal spoilers for Episode 13 of Arrow.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:53.580
I'm not gonna mention 'em here, but it has to do with what's going on with Oliver, and Laurel's, "Black Canaries".

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:54.080
So.

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:56.420
If you want to read about that, you can just go to IMDb.

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:59.940
I'm freaking excited about it, but it's just too spoilery to mention. 

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:04.460
So while you guys wait for The Flash tomorrow, you can click here* to learn about Gorilla Grodd in the comics.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:08.340
The producers said that he IS coming back in Season 1, but they didn't say which episode. 

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:11.540
And, you can click here* for last week's episode of Gotham.

00:09:11.540 --> 00:09:12.812
Thank you so much for watching.

00:09:12.812 --> 00:09:14.492
So, gorilla-sized high five. 

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:15.780
I'll see you guys tomorrow.

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:22.700
 

